+# Vendored RPCS3 RSX (Resistance 2 port)
+
+Origin: https://github.com/RPCS3/rpcs3 at commit `eee3f0f`, licensed GPLv2 (see `LICENSE`).
+Because of this code, the Resistance 2 port is distributed under the GPL.
+
+Files keep their original relative paths: `rpcs3/`, `Utilities/`, `3rdparty/`.
+**Every file here is unmodified unless it appears in the list below.**
+Edited lines are marked with `// R2PORT:`.
+
+## Modified vendored files
+
+| File | Change / reason |
+|---|---|
+| `rpcs3/util/types.hpp` | Under clang-cl, include `<intrin.h>`/`<immintrin.h>` instead of MSVC-only intrinsic forward declarations, which conflict with clang's builtins. |
+| `rpcs3/util/asm.hpp` | Inline-asm `_div128`/`_udiv128` for clang-cl, which lacks these MSVC intrinsics. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Common/BufferUtils_avx512.h` | The SIMD target-attribute guard is now `(_MSC_VER && !__clang__) \|\| !__SSE2__`, so clang-cl gets per-function `__attribute__((target))`. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Common/BufferUtils.cpp` | Same guard change for `SSE4_1_FUNC`/`AVX2_FUNC`/`AVX3_FUNC`. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/Memory/vm.h` | `g_base_addr`/`g_sudo_addr` are declared as `u8* const&`. They are bound to the port runtime's `vm_base`/`vm_sudo_base`, which are set after static initialization. |
+
+Many more RSX files carry `// R2PORT:` edits; `ps3recomp/patches/r2-rpcs3.patch` (R2 repo; `r3-rpcs3.patch` here) is the complete diff against `eee3f0f`. Perf/profiling edits (R2_RSX_PROF, see `r2rsx_bridge.cpp`):
+
+| File | Change / reason |
+|---|---|
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/port_prof.h` (new) | `r2prof::` counters for `R2_RSX_PROF=1`; no-op branches when off. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXThread.cpp` | Frame stats folded into `r2prof` at frame end; the `m_profiler` phase timers also run when profiling. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Core/RSXDisplay.h`, `VK/VKDraw.cpp` | `program_time`: `load_program` + `load_program_env` timed apart from setup. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Core/RSXCoreRenderer.cpp` | Draw wall time (begin .. post_draw_hook) and framebuffer-bind time. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKGSRender.cpp`, `RSXZCULL.cpp` | Counts/time of `flush_command_queue` (hard syncs), ZCULL host query reads, faults that need a GPU readback. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXFIFO.cpp` | FIFO empty: below 8 logical CPUs, `port_backoff` (pause, yield, then `Sleep(0)`) instead of yield-only spinning. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKPipelineCompiler.cpp` | `r2port::g_pipe_compiler_threads` sizes the auto compiler pool (set by the bridge from the CPU profile); workers are named "RSX.W shader" so the port's placement keeper runs them below normal priority. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKGSRender.cpp` (`on_framebuffer_bound`) | Round 2: the write-color-buffers copy is skipped when the surface being unbound is bound again by this bind (no readback can see it in between). `R2_FBB_KEEP_WCB=1` restores upstream. Sub-timers for the rebind (aa/dlss hooks, surface cache, WCB, locks, renderpass). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKQueryPool.cpp/.h` | Round 2: ZCULL query results are read in one `vkGetQueryPoolResults` call over the contiguous run of ended queries (`poke_query_run`); fault flush requests are served while waiting (`g_r2_query_wait_hook`). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXThread.cpp/.h`, `NV47/HW/nv47_sync.hpp`, `nv406e.cpp`, `rsx_methods.cpp`, `RSXZCULL.cpp/.h` | Round 3: deferred GCM labels (`R2_ZCULL_DEFER`, default on; `0` = upstream). A pipe-flushing label release that would block on the GPU for critical ZCULL reports is queued with the count of reports in front of it, and written from the main loop once `ZCULL_control::m_r2_retired` reaches it. Later labels queue behind it (order kept). `thread::sync()`, flip, NV406E acquire that would wait, renderer reset and exit drain the queue the upstream (blocking) way. Not used with relaxed ZCULL sync or host GPU labels. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKGSRender.cpp` (`get_occlusion_query_result`), `VKGSRenderTypes.hpp` | Round 3: a blocking ZCULL read sleeps on the command buffer's fence (`vkWaitForFences`, 250 µs slices, fault flushes served between) instead of spinning on query results. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Core/RSXGraphEngine.cpp`, `Program/ProgramStateCache.cpp` | Round 3: the program cache hint is dropped only on a ucode change/rehash; state-only changes are rechecked by `invalidate_*_program()` (`compare_properties`). `R2_PROG_HINT=0` = upstream. `cache_fragment_program` now copies `texcoord_centroid_mask`, which `compare_properties` checks. |
+| `port_prof.h`, `RSXThread.cpp`, `rsx_methods.cpp`, `nv3089.cpp`, `nv0039.cpp`, `VKDraw.cpp` | Round 3 profiling: rsx::thread self time outside draws (clears, fb-bind, ZCULL wait, flushes, labels, blits, flip command, housekeeping) and the DLSS/FSR hook time, so "busy excluding DLSS" can be tracked. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXThread.cpp/.h`, `rsx_methods.cpp` | Round 4: the flip no longer drains deferred ZCULL labels the blocking way. Labels queued during frame N are polled at flip N (non-blocking); only those older than `R2_ZCULL_FLIP_LAG` flips force the blocking drain, so the per-frame drain overlaps one frame of GPU work. Report values and label order are unchanged; a label may become visible up to one flip later. **Opt-in only, may hang:** the default is now `0` (round-3 behaviour, drain at every flip) after R3 bench r3c hung ~30 s into Haven with lag 1 and ran 3+ minutes clean with 0. While labels are carried, the main loop also drains them as soon as the FIFO is idle (the guest polling a label instead of feeding commands). |
+| `rpcs3/util/vm_native.cpp` (`memory_protect`) | Round 4: `R2_MM_SKIPSAME` (default on, `0` = upstream): `VirtualQuery` first and skip the `VirtualProtect` when the whole range already has that protection (texture-cache unprotect of pages a crushed deferred lock never protected). Counts calls/time/pages. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Host/MM.cpp/.h`, `RSXThread.cpp` (`renderctl`) | Round 4: the RSX Offloader drains the deferred-protect queue one block per lock hold (`mm_flush_incremental`) and yields when rsx::thread waits on the lock, instead of holding the queue lock over every `VirtualProtect`. `R2_MM_INCR=0` = upstream bulk flush. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Core/RSXGraphEngine.cpp` (`get_framebuffer_layout`) | Round 4, A/B only: `R2_FBB_KEEP=1` (default off) keeps a depth/colour target bound when the new layout would drop it as unused but it matches the bound one exactly, avoiding the rebind. Visual risk: a pass that samples the kept target becomes a feedback copy. |
+| `port_prof.h`, `VKGSRender.cpp`, `VKDraw.cpp`, `texture_cache.h`, `RSXDisplayEngine.cpp`, `vm_native.cpp`, `MM.cpp` | Round 4 profiling: fb-bind lock-phase split, texture-cache mutex/invalidation/relock counters, `VirtualProtect` calls and time, mm queue-lock wait, frame limiter vs present inside flip, program phase split (analyse, load_program, transform/fragment constants). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Common/texture_cache.h` (`invalidate_range_impl_base`) | Round 5: when a render target is committed over memory (`committed_as_fbo`, e.g. a depth buffer bound where a WCB-locked colour target lived), flushable sections lying entirely inside the new target's range are dropped as dirty instead of being read back (blocking GPU sync + copy, ~1 ms each); the new target's draws replace those bytes. Partially covered sections still flush. `R2_FBO_COMMIT_FLUSH=1` = upstream. Profiling: readback (`flush_set`) count/time, commit share, skipped sections; `load_program_env` split (DLSS/FSR draw hook, vertex/fragment/texture env, instancing, `bind_uniform`). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Core/RSXGraphEngine.cpp`, `VK/VKGSRender.cpp/.h` | Round 6 (from the R3 port): a re-sent fragment program whose address and instruction words (constants skipped) match the analysed one only re-uploads its constants (`R2_FP_REBIND=0` = upstream); a vertex program re-uploaded/re-selected with the same entry and transform-program words keeps its analysis (`R2_VP_REBIND=0` = upstream); both keep the program cache hint. When the hint still names the same two programs and the pipeline properties match the previous lookup, the previous pipeline is reused (`R2_PIPE_MEMO=0` = off). Counters: re-sent FP/VP kept, pipeline memo hits. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKGSRender.cpp/.h`, `RSXZCULL.cpp`, `rsx_methods.cpp`, `port_prof.h` | Round 6: ZCULL reports span many host occlusion queries. `check_occlusion_query_status` only tested the oldest, so the opportunistic `update()` (flip-time label poll, `set_active(false)`) read reports whose later queries were still running and the read slept on the command buffer fence until the GPU finished it: rsx::thread waited ~14 ms/frame inside the flip command in heli gameplay (GPU ~50% busy). The status check now requires what the read needs (a hit in an available query, unless precise counts, or every query available), and a read whose results are all available skips the flush and fence wait. Exact: values are unchanged, only reads that would block are left for a later poll. Forced reads (sync, read barrier, full pool) still wait. `R2_ZCULL_NOWAIT=0` = round-5 behaviour. Profiling: flip command split (label drain/ZCULL poll, `reset`, `on_frame_end`, emu flip, rest) and ZCULL reads answered without a wait vs waited (+time), by caller (update vs forced). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Program/ProgramStateCache.h` | R3 only: ucode MRU in front of the program maps (FP guest address + length, VP start + length; same equality as the map). `R2_PROG_MRU=0` = off. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Core/RSXCoreRenderer.cpp`, `RSXFIFO.cpp`, `RSXThread.cpp` | R3 only, diagnostics: `R2_DRAWLOG=<seconds>[:frames]` (per-draw state log, `R2_DRAWLOG_M=1` adds every method) and `R2_DRAWSTATS=1` (draws per frame). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKR2Upscaler.cpp` | R3 only: logical frame split for DLSS/FSR (`RSX_AA_SPLIT`, R3 renders the next frame's pre-pass before the flip). Relaxed ZCULL sync is the R3 default (set in the bridge; `R2_ZCULL=sync` = strict). |
+| `port_prof.h`, `Core/RSXCoreRenderer.cpp`, `Common/texture_cache.h`, `VK/VKGSRender.cpp` | Round 7 profiling: `now_ns` uses the invariant TSC (scaled once against QPC) instead of `steady_clock`, so the ~40 timestamps per draw disturb `R2_RSX_PROF` runs less. New counters: draw-window split (`begin` incl. fb-bind vs cond-render, `end` phases vs rest, methods between begin/end, post-draw tail), lock-phase internals (superseded invalidation, create+reprotect, fresh-lock reasons, superseded surfaces) and invalidation internals (intersection, unprotect, fast discards). Relaxed ZCULL sync is now the default on both ports (bridge; `R2_ZCULL=sync` = strict); the bridge profiler monitor caches its RSX thread handles, runs below normal priority and writes each 5 s block once (its own cost is printed on the `monitor:` line). No behaviour change with `R2_RSX_PROF` unset. |
+| FIFO recovery (rp9 crash) | `RSXFIFO.h/.cpp`, `RSXThread.cpp` | `recover_fifo` inside a method batch (`set_get(restore)` + `abort`) no longer lets `read_unsafe` step 4 bytes past the restored GET (upstream bug; with Atomic FIFO fetch the `ensure` in `fetch_u32` then killed rsx::thread). That `ensure` is now a logged resync. The "dead FIFO queue" path (20 recoveries < 2 s) skips GET to PUT and keeps running instead of throwing. Recoveries are logged (rate-limited) in rpcs3_rsx.log: `FIFO: recovering`, `out of step`, `dead command queue`. |
+
+## Not vendored / replaced (see `../rpcs3_shim`)
+
+- `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/GL/*`: excluded.
+- `rpcs3/Emu/System.cpp`: replaced by `emu_system_stub.cpp`.
+- `rpcs3/Emu/Memory/vm.cpp`: replaced by `vm_shim.cpp`.
+- `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXRendererFactory.cpp`: replaced by `rsx_renderer_factory.cpp` (no GL).
+- NP overlays (friends, trophies, messages): excluded.
+- zlib, ffmpeg/swscale, wolfssl, git-version: shim headers in `rpcs3_shim/include`.
+- Vulkan loader: the import library is generated from `rpcs3_shim/vulkan/vulkan-1.def`; no SDK is needed at link time.
+
+Extra third-party code not in the RPCS3 submodule set:
+- `3rdparty/Vulkan-Headers` (v1.4.344)
+- `3rdparty/pugixml` (1.15)
+
+## Build (standalone)
+
+Run inside a VS 2022 x64 developer environment with LLVM on PATH:
+
+```
+cmake -S ps3recomp\third_party\rpcs3 -B build_rpcs3 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang-cl -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang-cl
+cmake --build build_rpcs3 -j 8
+```
+
+Targets:
+- `rpcs3_rsx` (alias `rpcs3::rsx`): a static library.
+- `rpcs3_rsx_linktest`: a link check.
+
+The project can also be pulled in with `add_subdirectory(third_party/rpcs3)`.
+
+## Integration notes
+
+- The runtime must provide `extern "C" uint8_t* vm_base` and `vm_sudo_base`. `vm_sudo_base` is a second RW view of the same 4 GB.
+- Startup sequence:
+  1. Call `g_fxo->init()`, which resets and constructs the registered fxo objects.
+  2. Then call `rsx::create_render_thread(nullptr)`.
+  3. Set `g_emu_callbacks.get_gs_frame` before step 2.
+- `r2port::g_rsx_cache_dir` sets the shader cache dir. Leave it empty to disable the on-disk cache.
+- `rpcs3_shim/rsx_events_stub.cpp` holds `rsx::thread::send_event` and `sys_rsx_context_attribute`. Replace it with the real lv2 bridge.
